(Bug #59 in the call form LANGUAGE.md:419 documents - `<function> of each
 <var> from <collection> treating <match> as <replacement>`. A `value`
 parameter carries its argument's runtime tag across the call
 (LANGUAGE.md:2489-2493), so the tag the `treating` clause hands it has to
 be the element's own, not the integer default a tagless expression gets.)

To announce with a value called what.
  print what.

announce of each item from [1, "a"] treating "a" as "b".
announce of each item from [1, "a"] treating 1 as 9.
